@section [id="discussion"]:
  @heading [level=2]:
    Discussion
  @paragraph:
    Sustained autonomic tone is a precondition for tightly-coupled
    glucose-heart phase relationships. Loss of vagal influence under
    chronic hyperglycemia decouples the two oscillators; coherence
    falls long before HbA1c crosses any clinical threshold.
  @paragraph:
    A 90-second cohort screen using a wearable ECG patch and a single
    CGM hour could identify pre-diabetic decoupling years earlier than
    current laboratory criteria without a venous draw.

  @equation [id="eq-cpc" label="(1)"]:
    @latex:
      C_{xy}(f_1, f_2) = \frac{|\langle e^{i(\phi_x(f_1,t) - \phi_y(f_2,t))} \rangle_t|^2}{\langle |\phi_x|^2 \rangle \langle |\phi_y|^2 \rangle}
    @description:
      Cross-frequency phase coherence between signals x (glucose) and y (cardiac) at frequencies f1 and f2
